                <pb facs="1002" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg888"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Pickersgill, p. 551, states that the dinner party at the Citadel on August 18
                    (see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg840">p. 840</ref>) broke
                    up at midnight, after which Roosevelt, Churchill, and Mackenzie King “sat
                    together for quite a little time.” The Log, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg841">p. 841</ref>, indicates that Roosevelt and Churchill
                    held discussions after dinner “until another late retiring”. No record of the
                    discussions has been found.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
